<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The pre-Compose window background.

      It is one value with one job: the colour the window is painted the instant the activity is
      created, before Compose has drawn a frame. It is the light scheme's own `background` role —
      `Color.kt`'s `DeckPaper` — so the window never flashes a colour the theme does not paint, which
      is what makes the first frame invisible rather than a flicker.

      There is deliberately no seed colour here. A "seed" is a value a Material colour algorithm is
      fed, and this slot derives its palette by hand from its own subject rather than from a seed, so
      a `playkiln_seed` in this file would be a name that lies about where the colours come from.
      The identity itself lives in `store/studio.json` and in `ui/theme/Color.kt`, which is the one
      source of truth `scripts/core/palette.mjs` compares the pack against.
    -->
    <color name="playkiln_window_background">#F4FBFD</color>
</resources>
